Since person A alone completes $\frac{1}{a}$ of the project per hour, and person B alone completes $\frac{1}{b}$ of the project per hour, when they work together, the combined rate at which they complete the project per hour is:
$$\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b}$$
To find the total time taken for both A and B to complete the project together, we take the reciprocal of their combined rate:
\begin{align*}
\text{Total time} &= \frac{1}{\left(\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b}\right)} \\
&= \frac{1}{\frac{b + a}{ab}} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{ab}{a+b}}
\end{align*}

